0 Geared Four-Wheeled Car
0 Name: geared-car.ldr
0 Author: erik-larsen
0 // The simple car with two 8 tooth gears inside: rolling the car spins a second axle the
0 // other way. The base is two 1x8 plates under the side bricks, with nothing between them,
0 // so the gears don't catch a plate's studs (an 8 tooth gear 14 LDU above a plate would).
0 // The 1x4 bricks at each end tie the two plates together. Plate top at y=0 (LDraw -y is
0 // up); axles at y=-14; tyres touch the ground at y=17. Wheelbase 80 LDU (axles at x=+-40),
0 // track 100 LDU (wheel centres at z=+-50).

0 // Step 1: chassis: two 1x8 plates, 1x6 Technic bricks on them left and right, and 1x4
0 // Technic bricks front and back, across both plates
1 0 0 0 30 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3460.dat
1 0 0 0 -30 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3460.dat
1 14 70 -24 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3701.dat
1 14 -70 -24 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3701.dat
1 14 0 -24 30 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3894.dat
1 14 0 -24 -30 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3894.dat
0 STEP

0 // Step 2: 6L axles through the outermost holes of the 1x6 bricks, protruding 1 stud each side
1 0 40 -14 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3706.dat
1 0 -40 -14 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3706.dat
0 STEP

0 // Step 3: rim + tyre on each protruding axle end; left-side wheels turned 180 degrees to face outward
1 71 40 -14 50 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3482.dat
1 0 40 -14 50 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3483.dat
1 71 -40 -14 50 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3482.dat
1 0 -40 -14 50 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3483.dat
1 71 40 -14 -50 -1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 -1 3482.dat
1 0 40 -14 -50 -1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 -1 3483.dat
1 71 -40 -14 -50 -1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 -1 3482.dat
1 0 -40 -14 -50 -1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 -1 3483.dat
0 STEP

0 // Step 4: an 8 tooth gear on the rear axle, meshing with an 8 tooth gear on a 4L axle
0 // through the next holes of the 1x6 bricks. The second gear is turned half a tooth
0 // (22.5 degrees) to mesh.
1 72 -40 -14 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3647.dat
1 0 -20 -14 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3705.dat
1 72 -20 -14 0 0.92388 -0.382683 0 0.382683 0.92388 0 0 0 1 3647.dat
0 STEP

